"""Checks for the road-salt rationing season reports.

The expected reports are recomputed here, from the embedded copy of the shipped
extract, by a reference written for grading. Twenty-two further extracts are
built at grade time: eighteen by mutating that copy and four drawn fresh in the same
layout with new depots, order classes, calendars and daylight-saving periods.
The delivered program runs on each of them as an unprivileged user, through a
wrapper whose audit hook records every file it opens.

Negative checks are polarity-inverted: each returns True only when the failure it
names is positively observed, so honest work leaves them False.
"""
